    "summary": "PostgreSQL database adapter for Python -- C optimisation distribution"
   },
   "reviewed": {
    "by": "claude",
    "date": "2026-11-20",
    "earlier": [
     {
      "by": "claude",
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "note": "The bundled PostgreSQL client libraries: libpq, libkrb5, libldap and libcrypto import the network calls a database client needs (TLS, Kerberos, LDAP lookup of the service); libpq's popen is linked, never named in a URL or address; prctl names threads. No URLs or addresses. Content review only."
     }
    ],
    "note": "macOS arm64 and Windows amd64 wheels of the reviewed version. macOS: the delocated PostgreSQL client stack (libpq, OpenSSL 3, krb5, OpenLDAP) in .dylibs; Windows: delvewheel's libpq, libssl-3, libcrypto-3 and its os.add_dll_directory patch in __init__.py; _psycopg.c/pq.c differ only in the libpq build paths. The network imports (and libpq's popen) are those of a database client, as on Linux; no URLs or addresses beyond OpenSSL's. No .pth, no hook. No attestation, as for the Linux wheel: content review only."
   },
